<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  WinXL.targets of wxl @WXL_MSBUILD_VERSION@, written at install from cmake/WinXL.targets.in of the wxl
  tree (cmake/wxl_msbuild.cmake). NuGet imports it into a .vcxproj that references the package WinXL,
  after the project's own settings.

  The project builds the modules of wxl itself: the module interface units of wxl.core, fmt,
  wxl.highlight, wxl.bb and wxl.rsdn the package carries are compiled in it, with its own options,
  into BMIs alone (/ifcOnly: their code is in the archives of wxl), and MSBuild hands every source of
  the project the BMIs it imports (/reference), as it does with the std module. A BMI is tied to the
  compiler and the options that made it, so the package carries none.

  The archives of a link are those of the build of wxl made with the CRT the project compiles with
  (RuntimeLibrary): lib\md for the CRT in a DLL, lib\mt for the static one, the Debug archives for a
  debug CRT and the Release ones otherwise. A debug CRT and the iterator debugging of a Debug build go
  together, and the linker stops on a mix of either (LNK2038).

  The library of a profile is built in the project whose property WinXLProfile names the
  .winxl-profile, relative to the project or absolute, as wxl_add_ui_library of the CMake helpers
  builds it in an application on CMake. That project is a static library, the profile project of a
  solution, which every project on the WinUI layer references, or a program alone:

    the components  Read-ProfileComponents.ps1 of the helpers reads the chain of the profile and the
                    manifests of the components of the package (Windows PowerShell 5.1, before the
                    compile), and the sources of the selected components are compiled;
    the wrappers    winui-srcgen of the package writes them from the profile into
                    $(IntDir)WinXL\ui\<profile>\wxl, before the compile and only when the generator,
                    a profile, a manifest or the packages changed. It reads the packages from the
                    list Write-RestoredPackages.ps1 of the helpers writes from the restore of the
                    project and the metadata of the platform projection C++/WinRT makes in it, the
                    same text cmake/wxl_restored_packages.cmake writes on CMake;
    the library     the sources of the components and the parts of the wrappers are compiled with
                    the options of the project and those wxl_add_ui_library gives the library: in a
                    static library they are its archive, in a program they are archived into
                    $(IntDir)WinXL\wxl.ui.<profile>.lib, which it links;
    the interface   every other source of the project gets the include root of the wrappers, the
                    directories of the selected components and the headers of wxl.ui.common; a
                    static library gives them to the projects that reference it as its public
                    include directories (PublicIncludeDirectories), which MSBuild adds to their
                    sources, and names itself and its profile among what it tells them (an item of
                    FileType WinXLProfile in GetProjectInfoForReference).

  A program on the WinUI layer, one with WinXLProfile or one that references a profile project,
  links, besides the library of the profile, which MSBuild links from a reference
  (LinkLibraryDependencies), the archive of wxl.ui.common of its CRT, the system libraries of the
  layer and the import library of the bootstrapper of the Windows App Runtime; it takes the link
  options of wxl.ui.common and the Windows subsystem when it names none, and the DLLs a program on
  CMake gets beside it, the bootstrapper, Win2D and the loader of WebView2, are copied into
  $(OutDir) from its restore. A program stands on one profile project, and every project on the
  WinUI layer references it itself: a static library tells the projects that reference it the
  profile projects of its own references too, and a second profile project, or one reached through
  a library alone, stops the build before the wrappers are generated or anything is compiled.

  Every project compiles the module units of wxl for itself, and none of them gives its BMIs of
  them to the projects that reference it: each project imports the BMIs built with its own options.

  WinXLProfileParts sets the number of parts of the wrappers, as PARTS of wxl_add_ui_library does.

  Checked before the build:

    the toolset    $(VCToolsVersion) is @WXL_MSBUILD_TOOLS_VERSION@, the toolset of the archives, or
                   newer: a toolset links the archives of its own version and of older ones only. A
                   Visual Studio developer environment does not set the toolset of MSBuild: the project
                   names it, VCToolsVersion, or MSBuild takes the default of the installation.
    the language   every C++ source has the LanguageStandard and the options WinXL.props gives it: the
                   archives were compiled with them, and the code of wxl the project compiles (the
                   module units, the templates and inline functions it instantiates) has to agree
                   with them.
-->
<Project xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <WinXLToolsVersion>@WXL_MSBUILD_TOOLS_VERSION@</WinXLToolsVersion>
    <WinXLLanguageStandard>@WXL_MSBUILD_STANDARD@</WinXLLanguageStandard>
    <WinXLLanguageOptions>@WXL_MSBUILD_LANGUAGE_OPTIONS@</WinXLLanguageOptions>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- The build of wxl a source goes with, by its CRT, and what that build gives the code that uses it. -->
  <ItemDefinitionGroup>
    <ClCompile>
      <WinXLBuild Condition="'%(ClCompile.RuntimeLibrary)' == 'MultiThreadedDebugDLL' or '%(ClCompile.RuntimeLibrary)' == 'MultiThreadedDebug'">Debug</WinXLBuild>
      <WinXLBuild Condition="'%(ClCompile.RuntimeLibrary)' == 'MultiThreadedDLL' or '%(ClCompile.RuntimeLibrary)' == 'MultiThreaded'">Release</WinXLBuild>
      <PreprocessorDefinitions Condition="'%(ClCompile.WinXLBuild)' == 'Debug'">@WXL_MSBUILD_DEBUG_DEFINITIONS@;%(PreprocessorDefinitions)</PreprocessorDefinitions>
      <PreprocessorDefinitions Condition="'%(ClCompile.WinXLBuild)' == 'Release'">@WXL_MSBUILD_RELEASE_DEFINITIONS@;%(PreprocessorDefinitions)</PreprocessorDefinitions>
      <AdditionalOptions Condition="'%(ClCompile.WinXLBuild)' == 'Debug'">%(AdditionalOptions) @WXL_MSBUILD_DEBUG_OPTIONS@</AdditionalOptions>
      <AdditionalOptions Condition="'%(ClCompile.WinXLBuild)' == 'Release'">%(AdditionalOptions) @WXL_MSBUILD_RELEASE_OPTIONS@</AdditionalOptions>
    </ClCompile>
  </ItemDefinitionGroup>

  <!-- The module interface units, each with the directory of its BMI under $(IntDir)WinXL: two units
       of different directories may share a file name. -->
  <ItemGroup>
@WXL_MSBUILD_CORE_MODULES@@WXL_MSBUILD_FMT_MODULES@@WXL_MSBUILD_LIBRARY_MODULES@  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ClCompile Include="@(WinXLCoreModule)" />
    <!-- The unit of fmt with the definitions of its target in wxl, which are its own. -->
    <ClCompile Include="@(WinXLFmtModule)">
      <PreprocessorDefinitions>@WXL_MSBUILD_FMT_DEFINITIONS@;%(PreprocessorDefinitions)</PreprocessorDefinitions>
    </ClCompile>
    <!-- The units of wxl.highlight, wxl.bb and wxl.rsdn, the libraries beside wxl.core. -->
    <ClCompile Include="@(WinXLLibraryModule)" />
    <ClCompile Update="@(WinXLCoreModule);@(WinXLFmtModule);@(WinXLLibraryModule)">
      <CompileAs>CompileAsCppModule</CompileAs>
      <AdditionalOptions>%(AdditionalOptions) /ifcOnly</AdditionalOptions>
      <LinkCompiled>false</LinkCompiled>
      <LibCompiled>false</LibCompiled>
      <ImpLibCompiled>false</ImpLibCompiled>
      <ObjectFileName>$(IntDir)WinXL\%(WinXLDirectory)</ObjectFileName>
      <ModuleOutputFile>$(IntDir)WinXL\%(WinXLDirectory)</ModuleOutputFile>
      <ModuleDependenciesFile>$(IntDir)WinXL\%(WinXLDirectory)</ModuleDependenciesFile>
      <SourceDependenciesFile>$(IntDir)WinXL\%(WinXLDirectory)</SourceDependenciesFile>
      <PrecompiledHeader>NotUsing</PrecompiledHeader>
      <ForcedIncludeFiles />
      <CompileAsWinRT>false</CompileAsWinRT>
    </ClCompile>
  </ItemGroup>

  <Target Name="WinXLCheckToolset" BeforeTargets="PrepareForBuild">
    <Error Condition="!$([System.Text.RegularExpressions.Regex]::IsMatch('$(VCToolsVersion)', '^\d+\.\d+\.\d+$'))"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): the project names no MSVC toolset (VCToolsVersion is '$(VCToolsVersion)'). wxl is built with $(WinXLToolsVersion) and links with that toolset or a newer one: set VCToolsVersion in the project, or on the command line (-p:VCToolsVersion=...)." />
    <Error Condition="$([MSBuild]::VersionLessThan('$(VCToolsVersion)', '$(WinXLToolsVersion)'))"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): the project builds with the MSVC toolset $(VCToolsVersion), and wxl is built with $(WinXLToolsVersion): a toolset links archives of its own version and of older ones only. Install MSVC $(WinXLToolsVersion) or newer and name it in VCToolsVersion." />
  </Target>

  <Target Name="WinXLCheckLanguage" BeforeTargets="PrepareForBuild">
    <ItemGroup>
      <!-- The project's own C++ sources: the module units of wxl take the same settings, and naming
           them would bury the sources the project has to fix. -->
      <_WinXLCpp Include="@(ClCompile)" Condition="'%(ClCompile.WinXLDirectory)' == '' and '%(ClCompile.CompileAs)' != 'CompileAsC' and '%(ClCompile.Extension)' != '.c'" />
      <_WinXLWrongLanguage Include="@(_WinXLCpp)" Condition="'%(_WinXLCpp.LanguageStandard)' != '$(WinXLLanguageStandard)'">
        <WinXLWhat>LanguageStandard %(_WinXLCpp.LanguageStandard), not $(WinXLLanguageStandard)</WinXLWhat>
      </_WinXLWrongLanguage>
@WXL_MSBUILD_LANGUAGE_CHECKS@    </ItemGroup>
    <Error Condition="'@(_WinXLWrongLanguage)' != ''"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): sources of the project are compiled without the language of wxl, which WinXL.props sets (the LanguageStandard $(WinXLLanguageStandard) and the options $(WinXLLanguageOptions) in AdditionalOptions) and the project replaced: @(_WinXLWrongLanguage->'%(Filename)%(Extension): %(WinXLWhat)', '; ')." />
    <ItemGroup>
      <_WinXLCpp Remove="@(_WinXLCpp)" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!-- The manifest of a program on wxl, written for it from the template wxl_target_manifest() of the
       CMake helpers writes it from, with the name of the program in the identity
       (lib\cmake\wxl\helpers\wxl_app.manifest.in says what it holds and why). A project that brings a
       manifest of its own keeps it: two manifests with different identities do not merge. -->
  <Target Name="WinXLManifest" BeforeTargets="ComputeManifestInputsTargets"
          Condition="'$(ConfigurationType)' == 'Application' and '@(Manifest)' == ''">
    <PropertyGroup>
      <_WinXLManifest>$(IntDir)$(TargetName).wxl.manifest</_WinXLManifest>
      <_WinXLManifestText>$([System.IO.File]::ReadAllText('$(WinXLRoot)@WXL_MSBUILD_MANIFEST@').Replace('@WXL_MSBUILD_APP_NAME@', '$(TargetName)'))</_WinXLManifestText>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <WriteLinesToFile File="$(_WinXLManifest)" Lines="$([MSBuild]::Escape('$(_WinXLManifestText)'))"
                      Overwrite="true" WriteOnlyWhenDifferent="true" />
    <ItemGroup>
      <Manifest Include="$(_WinXLManifest)" />
      <FileWrites Include="$(_WinXLManifest)" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!-- Not for a static library: its archive would carry those of wxl, which the link of the program
       takes from the package. -->
  <Target Name="WinXLArchives" BeforeTargets="ComputeLinkInputsFromProject" DependsOnTargets="_WinXLUiProgram"
          Condition="'$(ConfigurationType)' == 'Application' or '$(ConfigurationType)' == 'DynamicLibrary'">
    <ItemGroup>
      <_WinXLRuntime Include="@(ClCompile->'%(RuntimeLibrary)'->Distinct())" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <Error Condition="'@(_WinXLRuntime->Count())' != '1'"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): the sources of the project are compiled with different CRTs (@(_WinXLRuntime, ', ')), and the archives of wxl are of one of them." />
    <PropertyGroup>
      <_WinXLRuntime>@(_WinXLRuntime)</_WinXLRuntime>
      <_WinXLVariant Condition="'$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreadedDLL' or '$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreadedDebugDLL'">md</_WinXLVariant>
      <_WinXLVariant Condition="'$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreaded' or '$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreadedDebug'">mt</_WinXLVariant>
      <_WinXLArchives Condition="'$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreadedDebugDLL' or '$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreadedDebug'">@WXL_MSBUILD_DEBUG_ARCHIVES@</_WinXLArchives>
      <_WinXLArchives Condition="'$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreadedDLL' or '$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreaded'">@WXL_MSBUILD_RELEASE_ARCHIVES@</_WinXLArchives>
      <!-- A program on the WinUI layer links wxl.ui.common too. -->
      <_WinXLUiArchives Condition="'$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreadedDebugDLL' or '$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreadedDebug'">@WXL_MSBUILD_DEBUG_UI_ARCHIVES@</_WinXLUiArchives>
      <_WinXLUiArchives Condition="'$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreadedDLL' or '$(_WinXLRuntime)' == 'MultiThreaded'">@WXL_MSBUILD_RELEASE_UI_ARCHIVES@</_WinXLUiArchives>
      <_WinXLArchives Condition="'$(_WinXLUiProgram)' == 'true' and '$(_WinXLArchives)' != ''">$(_WinXLArchives);$(_WinXLUiArchives)</_WinXLArchives>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <Error Condition="'$(_WinXLVariant)' == ''"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): the project compiles with the CRT '$(_WinXLRuntime)', and the archives of wxl are built with MultiThreaded, MultiThreadedDebug, MultiThreadedDLL or MultiThreadedDebugDLL." />
    <Error Condition="'$(_WinXLArchives)' == ''"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion) carries no archives of the configuration of wxl the CRT $(_WinXLRuntime) of the project links: the tree it was installed from was configured without it." />
    <ItemGroup>
      <_WinXLArchive Include="$(_WinXLArchives)" />
      <_WinXLArchive>
        <WinXLPath>$(WinXLRoot)@WXL_MSBUILD_LIB_DIR@\$(_WinXLVariant)\%(Identity)</WinXLPath>
      </_WinXLArchive>
    </ItemGroup>
    <Error Condition="!Exists('%(_WinXLArchive.WinXLPath)')"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion) has no %(_WinXLArchive.WinXLPath): the package carries no build of wxl made with the CRT $(_WinXLRuntime) the project compiles with." />
    <ItemGroup>
      <Library Include="@(_WinXLArchive->'%(WinXLPath)')" />
      <_WinXLArchive Remove="@(_WinXLArchive)" />
      <_WinXLRuntime Remove="@(_WinXLRuntime)" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!-- ==== The WinUI layer: the library of the profile WinXLProfile names, and the programs on it ==== -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <WinXLUi>@WXL_MSBUILD_UI@</WinXLUi>
    <!-- Directories without the trailing \, which on a command line would escape the closing quote. -->
    <_WinXLCommon>$(WinXLRoot)@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_INCLUDE_DIR@</_WinXLCommon>
    <_WinXLHelpers>$(WinXLRoot)@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_HELPERS@</_WinXLHelpers>
    <_WinXLIntDir>$([MSBuild]::NormalizeDirectory('$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)', '$(IntDir)', 'WinXL'))</_WinXLIntDir>
    <_WinXLPackages>$(_WinXLIntDir)restored-packages.json</_WinXLPackages>
    <_WinXLPowerShell>powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File</_WinXLPowerShell>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(WinXLProfile)' != ''">
    <WinXLProfileParts Condition="'$(WinXLProfileParts)' == ''">@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_PARTS@</WinXLProfileParts>
    <_WinXLProfile>$([MSBuild]::NormalizePath('$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)', '$(WinXLProfile)'))</_WinXLProfile>
    <_WinXLProfileName>$([System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension('$(_WinXLProfile)'))</_WinXLProfileName>
    <_WinXLProfileDir>$([System.IO.Path]::GetDirectoryName('$(_WinXLProfile)'))</_WinXLProfileDir>
    <_WinXLProfiles>$(WinXLRoot)@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_PROFILES@</_WinXLProfiles>
    <_WinXLComponents>$(WinXLRoot)@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_COMPONENTS@</_WinXLComponents>
    <_WinXLGenerator>$(WinXLRoot)@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_GENERATOR@</_WinXLGenerator>
    <!-- The include root of the generated headers, <wxl/X.h>, and the wrappers under it. -->
    <_WinXLUiRoot>$(_WinXLIntDir)ui\$(_WinXLProfileName)</_WinXLUiRoot>
    <_WinXLWrappers>$(_WinXLUiRoot)\wxl</_WinXLWrappers>
    <_WinXLProfileLibrary>$(_WinXLIntDir)wxl.ui.$(_WinXLProfileName).lib</_WinXLProfileLibrary>
    <BeforeClCompileTargets>$(BeforeClCompileTargets);WinXLProfileSources</BeforeClCompileTargets>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- What the library of the profile gives every source of its project, as its interface does on
       CMake; the directories of the selected components are added once the profile is read. -->
  <ItemDefinitionGroup Condition="'$(WinXLProfile)' != ''">
    <ClCompile>
      <AdditionalIncludeDirectories>%(AdditionalIncludeDirectories);$(_WinXLUiRoot);$(_WinXLCommon)</AdditionalIncludeDirectories>
    </ClCompile>
  </ItemDefinitionGroup>

  <!-- The files of the restored packages the layer stands on, found in the restore of the project. -->
  <ItemGroup>
@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_PACKAGE_FILES@  </ItemGroup>

  <Target Name="WinXLCheckProfile" BeforeTargets="PrepareForBuild" Condition="'$(WinXLProfile)' != ''">
    <Error Condition="'$(WinXLUi)' != 'true'"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion) is installed without the WinUI layer, and the project names the profile $(WinXLProfile)." />
    <Error Condition="'$(ConfigurationType)' != 'StaticLibrary' and '$(ConfigurationType)' != 'Application'"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): WinXLProfile names the profile whose library the project builds, and the project is a $(ConfigurationType): the library of a profile is built in a static library, which the projects on it reference, or in the one program that stands on it." />
    <Error Condition="!Exists('$(_WinXLProfile)')"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): WinXLProfile is '$(WinXLProfile)', and there is no profile $(_WinXLProfile)." />
    <Error Condition="'$(ProjectAssetsFile)' == '' or !Exists('$(ProjectAssetsFile)')"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): the project has no restore result of NuGet (ProjectAssetsFile is '$(ProjectAssetsFile)'), from which the generator of the wrappers takes the packages. A project on the WinUI layer references WinXL with a PackageReference, not with packages.config, and is restored first (msbuild -restore)." />
    <Error Condition="!$([System.Text.RegularExpressions.Regex]::IsMatch('$(WinXLProfileParts)', '^[0-9]+$')) or $(WinXLProfileParts) &lt; 1 or $(WinXLProfileParts) &gt; 100"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): WinXLProfileParts is '$(WinXLProfileParts)': the number of parts of the wrappers is from 1 to 100." />
  </Target>

  <!-- The components of the chain of the profile, closed over their dependencies: lines of the
       script, each of them an item. The script's output goes through a file, so that what it
       writes to the error stream is logged and not taken for a line. -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLProfileComponents">
    <MakeDir Directories="$(_WinXLIntDir)" />
    <Exec Command="$(_WinXLPowerShell) &quot;$(_WinXLHelpers)\Read-ProfileComponents.ps1&quot; -Profile &quot;$(_WinXLProfile)&quot; -ProfilesDir &quot;$(_WinXLProfiles)&quot; -ComponentDir &quot;$(_WinXLComponents)&quot; &gt; &quot;$(_WinXLIntDir)components.txt&quot;"
          EchoOff="true" UseUtf8Encoding="always" />
    <ReadLinesFromFile File="$(_WinXLIntDir)components.txt">
      <Output TaskParameter="Lines" ItemName="_WinXLComponentLine" />
    </ReadLinesFromFile>
    <ItemGroup>
      <FileWrites Include="$(_WinXLIntDir)components.txt" />
      <_WinXLComponentLine>
        <Kind>$([System.String]::Copy('%(Identity)').Split(':')[0])</Kind>
        <Value>$([System.String]::Copy('%(Identity)').Substring($([System.String]::Copy('%(Identity)').IndexOf(':'))).Substring(1).Replace('/', '\'))</Value>
      </_WinXLComponentLine>
      <_WinXLProfileFile Include="@(_WinXLComponentLine->WithMetadataValue('Kind', 'profile')->'%(Value)')" />
      <_WinXLChain Include="@(_WinXLComponentLine->WithMetadataValue('Kind', 'chain')->'%(Value)')" />
      <_WinXLComponentDir Include="@(_WinXLComponentLine->WithMetadataValue('Kind', 'dir')->'%(Value)')" />
      <_WinXLComponentSource Include="@(_WinXLComponentLine->WithMetadataValue('Kind', 'source')->'%(Value)')" />
      <_WinXLComponentLibrary Include="@(_WinXLComponentLine->WithMetadataValue('Kind', 'library')->'%(Value)')" />
      <_WinXLComponentLine Remove="@(_WinXLComponentLine)" />
      <_WinXLKnownLibrary Include="@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_COMPONENT_LIBRARIES@" />
      <_WinXLUnknownLibrary Include="@(_WinXLComponentLibrary)" Exclude="@(_WinXLKnownLibrary)" />
      <!-- The sources CMake compiles; the headers the manifests name are not. -->
      <_WinXLComponentSource>
        <WinXLCompile Condition="'%(Extension)' == '.cpp' or '%(Extension)' == '.cxx' or '%(Extension)' == '.cc'">true</WinXLCompile>
        <WinXLHeader Condition="'%(Extension)' == '.h' or '%(Extension)' == '.hpp' or '%(Extension)' == '.hxx' or '%(Extension)' == '.inl'">true</WinXLHeader>
      </_WinXLComponentSource>
      <_WinXLUnknownSource Include="@(_WinXLComponentSource)" Condition="'%(_WinXLComponentSource.WinXLCompile)' != 'true' and '%(_WinXLComponentSource.WinXLHeader)' != 'true'" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <Error Condition="'@(_WinXLUnknownLibrary)' != ''"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): components of the profile $(_WinXLProfileName) link @(_WinXLUnknownLibrary, ', '), and a project on MSBuild links the libraries of the package only (@(_WinXLKnownLibrary, ', '))." />
    <Error Condition="'@(_WinXLUnknownSource)' != ''"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): components of the profile $(_WinXLProfileName) name @(_WinXLUnknownSource, ', '), neither a C++ source nor a header." />
  </Target>

  <!-- The list of the restore the generator reads the packages from, and the directory of each
       package: the restore of the project, the version of the Windows SDK and the metadata of the
       platform projection C++/WinRT makes from it. -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLRestoredPackages" DependsOnTargets="GetCppWinRTPlatformWinMDInputs">
    <WriteLinesToFile File="$(_WinXLIntDir)platform-metadata.txt"
                      Lines="@(CppWinRTPlatformWinMDInputs->'%(WinMDPath)')"
                      Overwrite="true" WriteOnlyWhenDifferent="true" />
    <!-- Through a file, as the components above. -->
    <Exec Command="$(_WinXLPowerShell) &quot;$(_WinXLHelpers)\Write-RestoredPackages.ps1&quot; -Assets &quot;$(ProjectAssetsFile)&quot; -WindowsSdk &quot;$(TargetPlatformVersion)&quot; -Metadata &quot;$(_WinXLIntDir)platform-metadata.txt&quot; -Out &quot;$(_WinXLPackages)&quot; &gt; &quot;$(_WinXLIntDir)package-directories.txt&quot;"
          EchoOff="true" UseUtf8Encoding="always" />
    <ReadLinesFromFile File="$(_WinXLIntDir)package-directories.txt">
      <Output TaskParameter="Lines" ItemName="_WinXLPackageLine" />
    </ReadLinesFromFile>
    <ItemGroup>
      <FileWrites Include="$(_WinXLIntDir)package-directories.txt" />
      <_WinXLPackageLine>
        <Id>$([System.String]::Copy('%(Identity)').Split('|')[0])</Id>
        <PackageDirectory>$([System.String]::Copy('%(Identity)').Split('|')[1].Replace('/', '\'))</PackageDirectory>
      </_WinXLPackageLine>
      <_WinXLPackageDir Include="@(_WinXLPackageLine->'%(Id)')" />
      <_WinXLPackageLine Remove="@(_WinXLPackageLine)" />
      <FileWrites Include="$(_WinXLIntDir)platform-metadata.txt;$(_WinXLPackages)" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!-- The wrappers, written by the generator of the package when one of its inputs changed: the
       generator, the profile and the profiles beside it and among the generator's (a bare name in
       "extends" is looked for there), the manifests of the selected components, the packages. -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLWrapperInputs" DependsOnTargets="_WinXLProfileComponents;_WinXLRestoredPackages">
    <ItemGroup>
      <_WinXLWrapperInput Include="$(_WinXLGenerator);$(_WinXLProfile);$(_WinXLPackages);@(_WinXLProfileFile)" />
      <_WinXLWrapperInput Include="$(_WinXLProfileDir)\*.winxl-profile;$(_WinXLProfileDir)\types.json;$(_WinXLProfileDir)\fluent-symbols.json" />
      <_WinXLWrapperInput Include="$(_WinXLProfiles)\*.winxl-profile;$(_WinXLProfiles)\types.json;$(_WinXLProfiles)\fluent-symbols.json" />
      <_WinXLWrapperInput Include="@(_WinXLComponentDir->'%(Identity)\component.json')" />
      <!-- A name without a wildcard is an item whether or not the file is there, and a missing
           input would run the generator on every build. -->
      <_WinXLWrapperInput Remove="@(_WinXLWrapperInput)" Condition="!Exists('%(Identity)')" />
      <!-- The sources of the run the project compiles: the parts WinXLProfileParts asks for. -->
      <_WinXLPartNumber Include="@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_PART_NUMBERS@" />
      <_WinXLPart Include="@(_WinXLPartNumber->'$(_WinXLWrappers)\parts\wrapper-%(Identity).cpp')" Condition="%(Identity) &lt; $(WinXLProfileParts)" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <PropertyGroup>
      <_WinXLGeneratorCommand>&quot;$(_WinXLGenerator)&quot; --profile &quot;$(_WinXLProfile)&quot; --packages &quot;$(_WinXLPackages)&quot; --profiles-dir &quot;$(_WinXLProfiles)&quot; --types &quot;$(_WinXLProfiles)\types.json&quot; --symbols &quot;$(_WinXLProfiles)\fluent-symbols.json&quot; --out &quot;$(_WinXLWrappers)&quot; --parts $(WinXLProfileParts) --component-dir &quot;$(_WinXLComponents)&quot; @(_WinXLChain->'--component %(Identity)', ' ') --common-dir &quot;$(_WinXLCommon)&quot;</_WinXLGeneratorCommand>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <!-- The command itself is an input as well: another profile of the same name, another number
         of parts or another chain writes other wrappers from the same files. Written only when it
         changes, beside the wrappers and not among them. -->
    <WriteLinesToFile File="$(_WinXLUiRoot)\generator.command" Lines="$(_WinXLGeneratorCommand)"
                      Overwrite="true" WriteOnlyWhenDifferent="true" />
    <ItemGroup>
      <_WinXLWrapperInput Include="$(_WinXLUiRoot)\generator.command" />
      <FileWrites Include="$(_WinXLUiRoot)\generator.command" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <!-- The generator rewrites only the files that change, so the sources it writes cannot be the
         outputs of the run; the stamp is. A source of the run that is gone runs it again. -->
    <Delete Files="$(_WinXLWrappers)\generated.stamp" Condition="!Exists('%(_WinXLPart.Identity)')" />
  </Target>

  <Target Name="_WinXLWrappers" DependsOnTargets="_WinXLWrapperInputs"
          Inputs="@(_WinXLWrapperInput)" Outputs="$(_WinXLWrappers)\generated.stamp">
    <Exec Command="$(_WinXLGeneratorCommand)" />
    <Touch Files="$(_WinXLWrappers)\generated.stamp" AlwaysCreate="true" />
  </Target>

  <!-- Each file of the packages in the directory the restore put its package into. -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLPackageFiles" DependsOnTargets="_WinXLRestoredPackages">
    <ItemGroup>
      <!-- Batched by the package alone: the directory of the package of each file. -->
      <_WinXLPackageFile Include="@(WinXLPackageFile)" Condition="'%(Identity)' != '' and '@(_WinXLPackageDir)' != ''">
        <PackageDirectory>@(_WinXLPackageDir->'%(PackageDirectory)')</PackageDirectory>
      </_WinXLPackageFile>
      <_WinXLPackageFile>
        <WinXLPath>%(PackageDirectory)\%(Path)</WinXLPath>
      </_WinXLPackageFile>
      <_WinXLUnresolved Include="@(WinXLPackageFile)" Exclude="@(_WinXLPackageFile)" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <Error Condition="'@(_WinXLUnresolved)' != ''"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): the restore of the project resolved no @(_WinXLUnresolved->Distinct(), ', '), which the WinUI layer of wxl stands on." />
    <Warning Condition="'%(_WinXLPackageFile.Use)' != 'include' and !Exists('%(_WinXLPackageFile.WinXLPath)')"
             Text="No %(_WinXLPackageFile.WinXLPath) in the package %(_WinXLPackageFile.Identity); %(_WinXLPackageFile.Without)." />
  </Target>

  <!-- The sources of the library of the profile, compiled with the options of the project and what
       wxl_add_ui_library gives them, each object in a directory of its own under
       $(IntDir)WinXL\ui\<profile>\obj: a static library archives them as its own objects, a program
       archives them into the library it links. -->
  <Target Name="WinXLProfileSources" Condition="'$(WinXLProfile)' != ''"
          DependsOnTargets="_WinXLCheckProfiles;CppWinRTMakeProjections;_WinXLWrappers;_WinXLPackageFiles">
    <ItemGroup>
      <_WinXLCompiled Include="@(_WinXLComponentSource)" Condition="'%(_WinXLComponentSource.WinXLCompile)' == 'true'" />

      <ClCompile Include="@(_WinXLCompiled)">
        <WinXLProfileSource>true</WinXLProfileSource>
        <WinXLObject>$(_WinXLUiRoot)\obj\$([MSBuild]::MakeRelative('$(_WinXLComponents)\', '%(_WinXLCompiled.RootDir)%(_WinXLCompiled.Directory)'))%(_WinXLCompiled.Filename).obj</WinXLObject>
      </ClCompile>
      <ClCompile Include="@(_WinXLPart)">
        <WinXLProfileSource>true</WinXLProfileSource>
        <WinXLPart>true</WinXLPart>
        <WinXLObject>$(_WinXLUiRoot)\obj\parts\%(_WinXLPart.Filename).obj</WinXLObject>
      </ClCompile>

      <!-- Every source but the module units of wxl: the directories of the selected components. -->
      <ClCompile Condition="'%(ClCompile.WinXLDirectory)' == ''">
        <AdditionalIncludeDirectories>%(ClCompile.AdditionalIncludeDirectories);@(_WinXLComponentDir)</AdditionalIncludeDirectories>
      </ClCompile>
      <ClCompile Condition="'%(ClCompile.WinXLProfileSource)' == 'true'">
        <ObjectFileName>%(ClCompile.WinXLObject)</ObjectFileName>
        <PrecompiledHeader>NotUsing</PrecompiledHeader>
        <ForcedIncludeFiles />
        <AdditionalIncludeDirectories>%(ClCompile.AdditionalIncludeDirectories);@(_WinXLPackageFile->WithMetadataValue('Use', 'include')->'%(WinXLPath)')</AdditionalIncludeDirectories>
        <PreprocessorDefinitions>@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_DEFINITIONS@;%(ClCompile.PreprocessorDefinitions)</PreprocessorDefinitions>
      </ClCompile>
      <ClCompile Condition="'%(ClCompile.WinXLProfileSource)' == 'true' and '$(ConfigurationType)' == 'Application'">
        <LinkCompiled>false</LinkCompiled>
        <LibCompiled>false</LibCompiled>
      </ClCompile>
      <ClCompile Condition="'%(ClCompile.WinXLPart)' == 'true'">
        <AdditionalOptions>%(ClCompile.AdditionalOptions) @WXL_MSBUILD_UI_PART_OPTIONS@</AdditionalOptions>
      </ClCompile>
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!-- What the profile project gives the projects that reference it: the interface of the library
       as its public include directories, which MSBuild adds to the sources of each of them
       (ComputeReferenceCLInput), and its profile, by which a program knows it stands on the WinUI
       layer. The library itself a program links as the archive of a reference. -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLPublicIncludeDirectories" BeforeTargets="GetPublicIncludeDirectories"
          Condition="'$(WinXLProfile)' != '' and '$(ConfigurationType)' == 'StaticLibrary'"
          DependsOnTargets="_WinXLProfileComponents">
    <PropertyGroup>
      <PublicIncludeDirectories>$(PublicIncludeDirectories);$(_WinXLUiRoot);$(_WinXLCommon);@(_WinXLComponentDir)</PublicIncludeDirectories>
    </PropertyGroup>
  </Target>
  <!-- The item is the profile project itself, its profile a metadata: two profile projects are two
       profiles even when they name one .winxl-profile, and a project is one item however many ways
       lead to it. -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLProfileForReference" BeforeTargets="GetProjectInfoForReference"
          Condition="'$(WinXLProfile)' != '' and '$(ConfigurationType)' == 'StaticLibrary'">
    <ItemGroup>
      <ProjectInfoForReference Include="$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)">
        <FileType>WinXLProfile</FileType>
        <WinXLProfileFile>$(_WinXLProfile)</WinXLProfileFile>
      </ProjectInfoForReference>
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!-- The BMIs of the module units of wxl, all under $(IntDir)WinXL, stay in the project that built
       them: a project that references it compiles the units with its own options and imports those,
       and a module of two BMIs is ambiguous to the compiler (C7684). -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLPrivateModules" BeforeTargets="GetProjectInfoForReference">
    <ItemGroup>
      <ProjectInfoForReference Remove="@(ProjectInfoForReference)"
                               Condition="'%(ProjectInfoForReference.FileType)' == 'Module' and $([System.String]::Copy('%(ProjectInfoForReference.FullPath)').ToUpperInvariant().StartsWith('$(_WinXLIntDir.ToUpperInvariant())'))" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>


  <!-- A static library tells the projects that reference it the profile projects it stands on, those
       of its own references among them, as MSBuild tells them the archives of those references: a
       project learns of a profile project whose archive it links through a library. WinXLThrough
       names the library the project references, and each profile project is one item however many
       ways lead to it. Not at design time, where the references of the project are not yet known
       when the projects that reference it ask, and nothing checks the profiles. -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLForwardProfiles" BeforeTargets="GetProjectInfoForReference"
          DependsOnTargets="PrepareProjectReferences;GetReferencedVCProjectsInfo"
          Condition="'$(ConfigurationType)' == 'StaticLibrary' and '$(DesignTimeBuild)' != 'true'">
    <ItemGroup>
      <_WinXLForwardedProfile Include="@(ReferencedVCProjectsInfo->WithMetadataValue('FileType', 'WinXLProfile')->Distinct())" />
      <_WinXLForwardedProfile>
        <WinXLThrough>$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)</WinXLThrough>
      </_WinXLForwardedProfile>
      <ProjectInfoForReference Include="@(_WinXLForwardedProfile)" />
      <_WinXLForwardedProfile Remove="@(_WinXLForwardedProfile)" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!-- Whether the project is a program on the WinUI layer: one with WinXLProfile, or one that
       references a profile project. A program stands on one profile project, and every project on
       the layer references it itself: its include directories reach only the projects that reference
       it, and a program that links its archive through a library alone would link without
       wxl.ui.common. -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLUiProgram" DependsOnTargets="PrepareProjectReferences;GetReferencedVCProjectsInfo">
    <ItemGroup>
      <_WinXLReferencedProfile Include="@(ReferencedVCProjectsInfo->WithMetadataValue('FileType', 'WinXLProfile'))" />
      <_WinXLDirectProfile Include="@(_WinXLReferencedProfile)" Condition="'%(_WinXLReferencedProfile.WinXLThrough)' == ''" />
      <_WinXLIndirectProfile Include="@(_WinXLReferencedProfile)" Exclude="@(_WinXLDirectProfile)" />
      <_WinXLStandsOn Include="$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)" Condition="'$(WinXLProfile)' != ''">
        <WinXLProfileFile>$(_WinXLProfile)</WinXLProfileFile>
      </_WinXLStandsOn>
      <_WinXLStandsOn Include="@(_WinXLReferencedProfile->Distinct())" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <Error Condition="'@(_WinXLStandsOn->Distinct()->Count())' &gt; '1'"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): the project stands on the profile projects @(_WinXLStandsOn->Distinct()->'%(Identity) (%(WinXLProfileFile))', ', '): a program stands on one profile project, and every library in it on that one; a project that names its own profile in WinXLProfile references no profile project." />
    <Error Condition="'$(ConfigurationType)' == 'DynamicLibrary' and '@(_WinXLReferencedProfile)' != ''"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): the DLL links the library of the profile project @(_WinXLReferencedProfile->Distinct(), ', '), and the library of a profile is linked into the program that stands on it." />
    <Error Condition="'$(WinXLProfile)' == '' and '@(_WinXLDirectProfile)' == '' and '@(_WinXLIndirectProfile)' != ''"
           Text="WinXL $(WinXLVersion): the project links the library of the profile project @(_WinXLIndirectProfile->Distinct(), ', ') through @(_WinXLIndirectProfile->'%(WinXLThrough)'->Distinct(), ', ') and does not reference it: a project on the WinUI layer references the profile project itself, which gives it the include directories of the profile." />
    <PropertyGroup>
      <_WinXLUiProgram Condition="'$(ConfigurationType)' == 'Application' and ('$(WinXLProfile)' != '' or '@(_WinXLDirectProfile)' != '')">true</_WinXLUiProgram>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
      <_WinXLReferencedProfile Remove="@(_WinXLReferencedProfile)" />
      <_WinXLDirectProfile Remove="@(_WinXLDirectProfile)" />
      <_WinXLIndirectProfile Remove="@(_WinXLIndirectProfile)" />
      <_WinXLStandsOn Remove="@(_WinXLStandsOn)" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!-- The checks above, before the wrappers are generated (WinXLProfileSources depends on it) and
       before anything is compiled: a source that includes a header of the profile would otherwise
       stop first, on a header it cannot find. Not at design time (_WinXLForwardProfiles). -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLCheckProfiles" BeforeTargets="ClCompile" DependsOnTargets="_WinXLUiProgram"
          Condition="'$(DesignTimeBuild)' != 'true'" />


  <!-- The library of the profile a program builds, archived anew from the objects of its sources
       when one of them changed or the set of them did. -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLProfileLibrary" DependsOnTargets="_WinXLProfileObjects"
          Inputs="@(_WinXLProfileObject);$(_WinXLProfileLibrary).members" Outputs="$(_WinXLProfileLibrary)">
    <Delete Files="$(_WinXLProfileLibrary)" />
    <LIB Sources="@(_WinXLProfileObject)" OutputFile="$(_WinXLProfileLibrary)"
         SuppressStartupBanner="true" TrackFileAccess="false" ToolArchitecture="$(VCToolArchitecture)" />
  </Target>
  <Target Name="_WinXLProfileObjects">
    <ItemGroup>
      <_WinXLProfileObject Include="@(ClCompile->WithMetadataValue('WinXLProfileSource', 'true')->'%(ObjectFileName)')" />
      <FileWrites Include="$(_WinXLProfileLibrary).members" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <!-- The members, rewritten only when the set changes: an object no longer among them leaves
         the archive. -->
    <WriteLinesToFile File="$(_WinXLProfileLibrary).members" Lines="@(_WinXLProfileObject)"
                      Overwrite="true" WriteOnlyWhenDifferent="true" />
  </Target>
  <Target Name="_WinXLProgramProfileLibrary" Condition="'$(WinXLProfile)' != '' and '$(ConfigurationType)' == 'Application'"
          DependsOnTargets="_WinXLProfileLibrary">
    <ItemGroup>
      <Library Include="$(_WinXLProfileLibrary)" />
      <FileWrites Include="$(_WinXLProfileLibrary)" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>
  <!-- The files of the packages, found in the restore of the program, which has the packages of
       WinXL as the profile project has. -->
  <Target Name="_WinXLProgramPackageFiles" Condition="'$(_WinXLUiProgram)' == 'true'" DependsOnTargets="_WinXLPackageFiles" />

  <!-- What a program on the WinUI layer links besides the archives of wxl: the library of the
       profile it builds itself, the files of the packages the layer links, the system libraries of
       the layer and the link options of wxl.ui.common, and the Windows subsystem when it names
       none, as wxl_add_executable makes it on CMake: wxl owns its entry point. -->
  <Target Name="WinXLProgramLink" BeforeTargets="ComputeLinkInputsFromProject"
          DependsOnTargets="_WinXLUiProgram;_WinXLProgramProfileLibrary;_WinXLProgramPackageFiles"
          Condition="'$(ConfigurationType)' == 'Application'">
    <ItemGroup Condition="'$(_WinXLUiProgram)' == 'true'">
      <Library Include="@(_WinXLPackageFile->WithMetadataValue('Use', 'link')->'%(WinXLPath)')" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>
  <Target Name="WinXLProgramLinkOptions" BeforeTargets="Link" DependsOnTargets="_WinXLUiProgram"
          Condition="'$(ConfigurationType)' == 'Application'">
    <ItemGroup Condition="'$(_WinXLUiProgram)' == 'true'">
      <Link>
        <AdditionalDependencies>@WXL_MSBUILD_UI_LIBRARIES@;%(Link.AdditionalDependencies)</AdditionalDependencies>
        <AdditionalOptions>%(Link.AdditionalOptions) @WXL_MSBUILD_UI_LINK_OPTIONS@</AdditionalOptions>
        <SubSystem Condition="'%(Link.SubSystem)' == ''">Windows</SubSystem>
      </Link>
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!-- What a program on CMake gets beside it (wxl_target_runtime), copied into $(OutDir). -->
  <Target Name="WinXLRuntimeFiles" AfterTargets="Link" DependsOnTargets="_WinXLUiProgram;_WinXLProgramPackageFiles"
          Condition="'$(ConfigurationType)' == 'Application'">
    <ItemGroup Condition="'$(_WinXLUiProgram)' == 'true'">
      <_WinXLRuntimeFile Include="@(_WinXLPackageFile->WithMetadataValue('Use', 'runtime')->'%(WinXLPath)')" />
      <_WinXLRuntimeFile Remove="@(_WinXLRuntimeFile)" Condition="!Exists('%(Identity)')" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <Copy SourceFiles="@(_WinXLRuntimeFile)" DestinationFolder="$(OutDir)" SkipUnchangedFiles="true">
      <Output TaskParameter="CopiedFiles" ItemName="FileWrites" />
    </Copy>
  </Target>
</Project>
